# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Scene hl2-tanks (test/README.md): hldemo2's mounted guns and trailer-yard
# mortars (game/hl/tanks.c; HLSDK func_tank.cpp, mortar.cpp, rpg.cpp), as
# test/m5/tanks.route with views and a stats window: the player in the yard
# north of the sandbag nest, sandbag_gun_1 (func_tank, 12 mm, 10 rounds/s,
# muzzle flash sprites) and missile_turret (func_tankrocket, rpg_rocket,
# steam smoke sprites) tracking and firing at him; then the player on
# biggun (+use on its func_tankcontrols, view-steered, firing); then the
# yard's trigger_once *82 -> init_trailer_mortars_mm: four
# func_mortar_field strikes (lightning beam, explosion, shake) on the
# trailers, the first 5.5 s after the trigger. New Game on hldemo2 (no
# uplink.route window: the route walks the yard's north side and leaves
# by the east yard without facing the nest).
startmap hldemo2
waitmap hldemo2 60
god 1
setpos 2300 400 -60 0 270
wait 0.5
stats begin
waitmoved sandbag_gun_1 8
waitclass rpg_rocket 2445 182 -35 400 10
wait 0.3
shot tanks-fire
# the rocket ignites 0.4 s after launch: its trail (TE_BEAMFOLLOW) and
# EF_LIGHT from the turret toward the player
wait 0.6
shot rocket-trail
wait 0.9
stats tanks-fire
# biggun: its controls (x 2372..2380, y 37..103) ahead
setpos 2355 70 -40 0 0
wait 1
+use
wait 0.2
-use
look 5 20
waitmoved biggun 5
+attack
wait 0.5
shot biggun-fire
wait 1
-attack
stats biggun
setpos 2300 400 -60 0 270
wait 1
# trigger_once *82 (delay 3): mortar field *81 (x 2616..2664, y 488..536)
# strikes 5.5 s later, *83 / *86 / *87 a second apart each
setpos 1830 1072 -60 0 0
look -10 -34
wait 5.55
shot mortar-1
wait 4
stats end
pass
